January 31, 2026
We are building a very rare type of application:
it is not a fitness tracker
it is not an alarm clock
it is not meditation
It is a distributed sleep resonance system.
We decided to build the network based on telemetry transmission via MQTT.
Everything seems to be ready. 
In subsequent versions, I will work on the UI. For now, there is a slight gap in this area. Everything looks like a terminal from the 1980s.

January 23, 2026.
BioKey Architectural Plan (v0.1 — Current Status)
1. Sensor and Capture Layer (Data Acquisition):
Audio Capture: Background recording (PCM), low-frequency amplitude extraction.
Motion Capture: Accelerometer, calculation of the “Rest Index.”
Sync Manager: Synchronization with atomic clocks (NTP) — our “tuning fork.”
2. Analytical layer (Logic Engine):
WaveCore: Schumann mathematics, lunar phases, geo-intensity (40°).
SleepSignalProcessor: Our new “filter.” Divides the signal into frequencies, searches for 0.15–0.4 Hz (breathing).
Wave Fidelity Logic: Calculates “Fidelity” — the percentage of confidence that the user is truly in deep sleep.
3. Execution layer:
BioWaveService: The very same “Guard” (Foreground Service) that keeps everything in memory.
DeepSleep Hook: Intelligent trigger for starting the installation (4:30 a.m.).
BioAudioEngine: Binaural synthesizer + TTS (Voice).
4. Presentation layer (UI):
Terminal UI: Green CLI interface “Sarah Connor” with real-time telemetry and logs.

Development plan: What remains before release
Step 1: LOGIC-12 — Calibration and UI Finalization
We need the terminal to stop displaying “placeholders” and show the actual BPM and Fidelity. This is critical for visual confirmation of 30 years of research.
Step 2: LOGIC-13 — Energy Efficiency (Battery Guard)
The device should not “burn out” or run out of power by morning. We will configure an adaptive sensor polling frequency: if the user is stationary, we slow down; if movement begins, we speed up.
Step 3: LOGIC-14 — Data Export and Sovereignty
We finalize SleepPatternPacker. We will generate the very “digital asset” (QR/File) that the user can take with them.
Step 4: SYNC-3 — GunDB & P2P (Global Wave)
Final chord v0.1: launch a decentralized network so that “Beacons” from Panama can see “Beacons” from the Dominican Republic, the US, Canada, Japan, Korea...



